      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to use the fact that the roots of the polynomial \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0\\) are \\(3\\), \\(-2\\), and \\(r\\). By Vieta's formulas, the sum of the roots of the polynomial \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0\\) is given by \\(-\\frac{b}{a}\\). Therefore, we have:\n\n\\[\n3 + (-2) + r = -\\frac{b}{a}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the left side, we get:\n\n\\[\n1 + r = -\\frac{b}{a}\n\\]\n\nThis can be rewritten as:\n\n\\[\nr = -\\frac{b}{a} - 1\n\\]\n\nNext, we use the product of the roots taken two at a time, which is given by \\(\\frac{c}{a}\\). Therefore, we have:\n\n\\[\n3 \\cdot (-2) + 3 \\cdot r + (-2) \\cdot r = \\frac{c}{a}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the left side, we get:\n\n\\[\n-6 + 3r - 2r = \\frac{c}{a}\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n-6 + r = \\frac{c}{a}\n\\]\n\nWe already know that \\(r = -\\frac{b}{a} - 1\\), so substituting this into the equation, we get:\n\n\\[\n-6 + \\left(-\\frac{b}{a} - 1\\right) = \\frac{c}{a}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the left side, we get:\n\n\\[\n-6 - \\frac{b}{a} - 1 = \\frac{c}{a}\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n-7 - \\frac{b}{a} = \\frac{c}{a}\n\\]\n\nMultiplying both sides by \\(a\\) to clear the fraction, we get:\n\n\\[\n-7a - b = c\n\\]\n\nRearranging the terms, we get:\n\n\\[\nc = -7a - b\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\(\\frac{b+c}{a}\\). Substituting the expression for \\(c\\) into this, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{b+c}{a} = \\frac{b + (-7a - b)}{a} = \\frac{b - 7a - b}{a} = \\frac{-7a}{a} = -7\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\frac{b+c}{a}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-7}\n\\]",
